  "answer": "[`applyProcessingState`](/Users/Shared/nav-ab/p0-domain-context-ng1ni/src/marketing/status.ts:9) accepts a record, a new state (`\"draft\" | \"scheduled\" | \"sending\" | \"complete\"`), and a `publish` callback.\n\nIt assigns the state to `record.processingState`, then immediately publishes this frame:\n\n```ts\n{\n  resource: {\n    id: record.campaignId,\n    processing_status: record.processingState\n  },\n  type: \"marketing_campaign\",\n  event: \"status_changed\"\n}\n```\n\nThere’s no validation or equality check: every call updates the record and publishes the frame, even if the state is unchanged.",
